                        <provenance>The scroll belonged to <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15604WalattaGab">Walatta Gabrǝʾel</persName>. According to
                            the account on the manuscripts’ provenance given by Tisserant, this
                            manuscript is among those acquired by <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4805Grebaut">Sylvain Grébaut</persName> in <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC1216AddisA">ʾAddis
                                ʾAbabā</placeName> in <date when="1925"/> with funds of <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS14055SaintJ">Jean Saint</persName>. The manuscripts
                            originate from <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC0241IHA">Šawā</placeName> (ʾAddis
                            ʾAbabā, <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC2297DabraL">Dabra Libānos</placeName>,
                                <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC2246DabraB">Dabra Bǝrhān</placeName>), <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC3549Gojjam">Goǧǧām</placeName> (<placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC2687DimaG">Dimā Giyorgis</placeName>, <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC7140Martula">Marṭula Māryām</placeName>, <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC6927DabraWarq">Dabra Warq</placeName>) and <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC1713Bagemd">Bagemdǝr</placeName> (<placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC3577Gondar">Gondar</placeName>, <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC1669Azazo">ʾAzazo Takla Hāymānot</placeName>) and a few from
                                <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC6569Tegray">Tǝgrāy</placeName>.</provenance>
                    </history>
